# The agent's own environment. Copy to .env next to this file; `mda dev` and
# `mda deploy` read it. Values come from the root .env (`bun run okta-setup`
# and `bun run setup-arcade` write them there) and from your LangSmith workspace.
# In the workshop the values come from the attendee portal, and its "Start your agent" step
# shows the block to paste.

# --- Required -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Deploys and runs the agent on Managed Deep Agents (needs the MDA beta).
LANGSMITH_API_KEY=
# The same Arcade project key as the root .env.
ARCADE_API_KEY=
# The identity provider, the same value as the root .env: an Okta custom
# authorization server, e.g. https://<org>.okta.com/oauth2/default. The keys
# that verify callers are the ones its discovery document names.
IDP_ISSUER=
# The Okta app `bun run okta-setup` created, from the root .env. The id is the
# audience of the ID tokens callers send; ask.py signs in as this app, so it
# needs the secret.
IDP_CLIENT_ID=
IDP_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Optional -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Where ask.py sends the run. Blank, `mda dev`'s local server.
# AGENT_URL=
# Your own email, for a room where the Okta sign-in is a shared persona: the
# loan desk runs as the persona, Gmail and Slack as this address. The same as
# `ask.py --as`. It must be the email of your Arcade account, invited to the
# project, with a subject (`bun run users add ... --no-identity`).
# CONNECTED_APPS_USER=
# A real model instead of the scripted one. Its package goes in pyproject's
# dependencies: that is what `mda dev` and `mda deploy` build from.
# MODEL_ID=openai:gpt-5.5
# Its key, one of two ways. The provider's key here:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Or none on this machine: every model call goes through the LangSmith LLM Gateway,
# signed in with the key below, whose workspace holds the provider key as a secret.
# In the workshop that key is the room's, from portal step 2.
# LANGSMITH_GATEWAY=true
# LANGSMITH_GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# --- Module 04: evals (evals/, docs/modules/04-observe.md) --------------------
# Who the eval runs as: your own email, the one ask.py signs in as.
# EVAL_LOAN_OFFICER=
# The tracing project this morning's runs are in. `mda dev` traces to loan-desk-local.
# EVAL_PROJECT=loan-desk-local
# The judge's model, in the notebook and in the online rule. Blank, MODEL_ID. The online
# rule reads its key from a workspace secret: LANGSMITH_GATEWAY_API_KEY with the gateway
# lines set, otherwise OPENAI_API_KEY or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
# JUDGE_MODEL=
# The repo's own app, for audit rows beside a trace. In the workshop, live activity has them.
# APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
